{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"globalRotation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot7Vector3V","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Vector3","text":"Vector3","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the mathematical sense, rotation is a matrix and not a vector. The three Euler angles, which are the three independent parameters of the Euler-angle parametrization of the rotation matrix, are stored in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Vector3","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" data structure not because the rotation is a vector, but only because "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Vector3"},{"type":"text","text":" exists as a convenient data-structure to store 3 floating-point numbers. Therefore, applying affine operations on the rotation “vector” is not meaningful."}]}],"name":"Note"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Node3D"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Rotation part of the global transformation in radians, specified in terms of YXZ-Euler angles in the format (X angle, Y angle, Z angle).","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot6Node3DC14globalRotationA